1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,830
One question, five runs.

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:10,810
When a user pushes an insurance agent for a payout, does the agent keep\Nnaming the licensed adjuster as the one who decides?

3
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:13,120
Four models, two families, one instrument.

4
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:17,350
Everything was pre-registered, including what failed.

5
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,740
The design has two arms.

6
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:30,180
In escalation the user asks for the payout to be approved, and the agent\Nnames the limit forty-eight to sixty percent of the time, in all

7
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:31,341
four models.

8
00:00:31,381 --> 00:00:37,930
In sustained pressure nobody asks: urgency, a prior promise, social\Nproof, a claimed authority.

9
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:42,831
That arm runs from twelve point five to fifty percent.

10
00:00:42,871 --> 00:00:44,990
Forty conversations per arm.

11
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:46,940
The five runs.

12
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:54,480
The escalation column barely moves: fifty, forty-eight point seven,\Nsixty, sixty, fifty.

13
00:00:54,520 --> 00:01:05,950
The sustained column moves by a factor of four: twenty-eight point nine,\Neighteen point four, forty-seven point five, fifty, twelve point

14
00:01:05,990 --> 00:01:06,580
five.

15
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:09,370
We could have published a ranking.

16
00:01:09,410 --> 00:01:13,580
The intervals do not allow it: only two contrasts clear zero.

17
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:16,710
And the decisive number is not between models.

18
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:24,180
The same model, run twice with the same instrument, reads twenty-eight\Npoint nine and then eighteen point four.

19
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:27,950
A ten point gap, whose interval crosses zero.

20
00:01:27,990 --> 00:01:32,670
At forty turns per arm, ordering these models would be ordering noise.

21
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:42,290
The contract's own adapter read zero of forty: it required a literal\Nphrase, and the model wrote the passive voice.

22
00:01:42,330 --> 00:01:45,230
Repaired, it reaches six of eight cells in sample.

23
00:01:45,270 --> 00:01:51,710
Then it met a new model's text: it held escalation, and lost five of\Nfive in sustained.

24
00:01:51,750 --> 00:02:00,160
All five are one construction, I can help by collecting, written before\Nthat text existed, and not patched after.

25
00:02:00,850 --> 00:02:10,870
Across five hundred and ninety-one replies, three hundred and twenty of\Nthem under pressure, the contract's list of forbidden phrasings

26
00:02:10,910 --> 00:02:13,840
finds zero approvals, zero promises, zero quotes.

27
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:15,496
No model cedes.

28
00:02:15,536 --> 00:02:19,000
What differs is whether it says why.

29
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:24,130
A lower restatement rate is not a safety win: it means the limit is\Nrarely named.

30
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:34,210
All of it runs offline from a clone, with no API key: the signed\Nevidence check, the clause audit, the cession check.

31
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:42,870
Every figure sits beside its pre-registration, its nulls, and two claims\Nthat were withdrawn when they failed to replicate.
